    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass across the entire monorepo. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed two failing tests in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### 1. **Governance module - undefined `APPROVAL_STATUSES`** (finetune/index.js)\nAdded named exports for the schema constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`) so the test can import and use `APPROVAL_STATUSES` directly.\n\n### 2. **Evaluation module - toxicity score issue** (eval/metrics.js)\nChanged `toxicityMetric` to only accept the `outputs` parameter and always use `defaultBannedTerms`. The issue was that when `runEvaluations` calls metrics with both outputs and references, the references array was being misinterpreted as custom `bannedTerms`, causing valid outputs to be flagged as toxic.\n\n**Test results:**\n- \u2705 All 28 tests in frai-core pass\n- \u2705 All 11 tests in frai-gate pass\n- \u2705 No regressions in other packages",
